---
import Layout from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About — High Signal Podcasts"
  description="Why High Signal Podcasts indexes source-backed claims instead of episodes, and how to contact the project."
>
  <section class="info-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the index</p>
    <h1>A listening shortcut that leaves the source intact.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      High Signal Podcasts is a High Signal project for finding attributable ideas and
      recommendations in long public conversations. It organizes the useful unit—the claim—while
      preserving the exact excerpt, speaker, date, and source trail.
    </p>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <article><p class="folio">Purpose / 01</p><h2>Find the line that matters.</h2><p>Search people, claims, books, tools, and products without treating a full episode as the smallest useful result.</p></article>
      <article><p class="folio">Boundary / 02</p><h2>Missing is better than invented.</h2><p>The public-beta corpus is deliberately bounded. Unknown speakers and low-confidence evidence stay unpublished.</p></article>
      <article><p class="folio">Ownership / 03</p><h2>Built in the open.</h2><p>The project source and its evidence contract are public. Product questions and corrections can be raised on GitHub.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="info-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/Significant-Hobbies/on-record/issues">Contact via GitHub ↗</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/methodology">Read the methodology</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
